    "c2": {
      "anchor": "i234",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "Links in the chat open in the browser; a side bar link leaves no tab behind",
      "excerpt": "Links in the chat open in the browser; a side bar link leaves no tab behind",
      "text": "In VSC, when I click a sidebar link, it will show in the sidebar, but the top window in chrome reloads its current page",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-10T00:42:48.142Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-10T00:44:13.375Z",
          "html": "<p>Side bar links reach Chrome because the <code>workbench.externalUriOpeners</code> setting from r61 sends every local link there. Chrome opens a tab for the link, the tab closes itself, and the page you were on loses and regains focus. Why it then reloads isn't confirmed: a page that's out of date reloads as soon as it's hidden, which fits but wasn't reproduced.</p>\n<p>Recommended: remove that setting. Side bar links then never touch Chrome, and the 🌐 link still opens Chrome, because the page server does that itself. The cost is the brief VS Code tab from r61, which the extension closes at once.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-10T00:44:11.810Z"
      }
    }
  },
  "on": {}
}
